# Simple ALU

## Goal

Build a simple Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU) in Verilog that can perform arithmetic, logical and shift operations.

The ALU is one of the most important building blocks inside a CPU because it performs operations on data provided by the processor.

---

# What is an ALU?

An ALU (Arithmetic Logic Unit) is a digital circuit that performs mathematical and logical operations.

A simplified CPU datapath can be represented as:

             ┌───────────────┐
             │ Register File │
             └───────┬───────┘
                     │
                ┌────┴────┐
                │         │
                ▼         ▼
             Operand A  Operand B
                │         │
                └────┬────┘
                     ▼
                ┌─────────┐
                │   ALU   │
                └────┬────┘
                     │
                     ▼
                  Result

The ALU receives operands and an operation control signal and produces a result.

